  "id": "19e4de28-7488-5db3-91c5-3c806815e2ba",
  "slug": "chicken-tequila-fettuccini",
  "name": "Chicken Tequila Fettuccini",
  "recipe_type": "main",
  "brief_description": "Red, yellow and green bell peppers reflect the vibrancy of this creamy chicken fettucini with jalapenos, garlic and cilantro. Tequila and lime give a unique finish.",
  "cuisine": "U.S.",
  "instructions": [
    {
      "position": 1,
      "text": "In a medium saucepan, saute the cilantro, garlic and jalapeno pepper in 2 tablespoons of butter or margarine over medium heat for 4 to 5 minutes. Add the stock, tequila and lime juice. Bring the mixture to a boil and cook until reduced to a paste-like consistency. Set aside."
    },
    {
      "position": 2,
      "text": "Pour soy sauce over the chicken and set aside for 5 minutes. Meanwhile, In a medium sized skillet, saute the onion and the red, green and yellow bell peppers with the remaining tablespoon of butter or margarine, stirring occasionally."
    },
    {
      "position": 3,
      "text": "Meanwhile, cook fettuccini according to package directions."
    },
    {
      "position": 4,
      "text": "When the peppers have wilted, add the chicken and soy sauce. Toss and add the reserved tequila/lime paste and cream. Bring to a boil. Gently simmer until chicken is cooked through and sauce is thick. Toss with well drained fettuccini and garnish with cilantro. Serve."
    }
  ],
  "servings": 4,
